"/CONTRIBUTING-32","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"Every major section has an `index.md`. Keep existing published slugs (`getting-started`,\n`architecture`, …): the route is the file path without its extension, so renaming a file\nbreaks every bookmark and README link to it. Put **new** pages under `start/`, `learn/`,\n`concepts/`, `operate/`, `contribute/`."},"212":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-33","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"A new page needs three things or it will not appear in the sidebar and the coverage gate\nfails: the file under `docs/`, an entry in the nav (see above), and a listing in\n`_HAND_WRITTEN_MD` in `docs/BUILD.bazel` so Bazel ships it as a runfile."},"213":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-34","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"Use the right-hand ToC for long pages. Keep navigation focused."},"214":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-35","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Every page must open (after the title or any intentional top widget such as the interactive panel) with a scannable overview in this bullet-point format:\n**What's on this page**"},"215":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-36","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Bullets describing the main content, sections, diagrams, tables, etc.\n**What this enables / practical use**"},"216":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-37","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Bullets describing reader benefit, common use cases, or what the content lets you achieve."},"217":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-38","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Write for humans. Be concise. Remove filler."},"218":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-39","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Include copy-pasteable examples."},"219":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-40","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Use Mermaid for diagrams (supported)."},"220":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-41","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Prefer `<Callout type=\"info|warning|error\" title=\"…\">` for asides and `<Tabs>`/`<Tab>` for\nalternatives. The `!!!` and `=== \"Title\"` syntax is **not** parsed any more — the migration\nrewrote existing uses, and new content uses the components directly (see\n`docs-site/components/mdx-components.tsx` for what is importable)."},"221":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-42","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Pages that need those components are `.mdx`; pages that do not can stay `.md`. Both are\nvalid MDX, so plain Markdown keeps working unchanged."},"222":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-43","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Escape what MDX would otherwise read as JSX: a literal `<` in prose or code needs `&lt;`,\n